# 🔴 .gitignore MUST CHECK OUT AS LF, whatever the machine's autocrlf says — this is a correctness
# rule, not a style one. GitHub's Windows runners set autocrlf, so a fresh clone there materialized
# the (LF-committed) .gitignore as CRLF, an EMPTY line became a lone CR, and git's ignore parser
# treats a lone-CR line as a pattern matching EVERY directory. `git check-ignore <anything>/`
# answered "ignored" for the whole tree, the doc-drift citation scanner believed it, and the release
# stopped on 1,600 findings about prose that was fine. Minimal repro, git 2.53:
# a .gitignore of `bin/\r\n` + `\r\n` calls `zzz/qqq/` ignored, attributed to the blank line.
.gitignore text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Markdown checks out as LF too: the gates compare generated text against these files, and an
# autocrlf checkout failing a comparison every LF checkout passes is this same class again —
# decisions-index was the second victim after .gitignore. (Its checker now also normalizes, so this
# line is the belt and that is the braces.)
*.md text eol=lf

